<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus Airways has 2.1 mln pre-tax 96 loss.</title>
<headline>Cyprus Airways has 2.1 mln pre-tax 96 loss.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results for year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In thousands of Cyprus pounds unless stated)</p>
<p>					     1996		1995</p>
<p>    Turnover			   124,481	    130,135</p>
<p>Profit from operations before</p>
<p>charging depreciation and</p>
<p>    interest			    18,402	     30,115</p>
<p>    Depreciation			15,895	     15,691</p>
<p>    Interest			     7,750		9,389</p>
<p>(Loss) profit of the group</p>
<p>before taxation and</p>
<p>    extraordinary item		(5,243)	     5,035</p>
<p>    Extraordinary item*		2,627		  --</p>
<p>(Loss) profit of the group</p>
<p>before taxation and after</p>
<p>inclusion of extraordinary</p>
<p>    item				  (2,616)	     5,035</p>
<p>    Profit of duty free shops*	  483		--</p>
<p>(Loss)/profit of group before</p>
<p>    tax				    (2,133)	    5,035</p>
<p>    Tax					 199	     1,229</p>
<p>    (Loss)/profit after tax	  (2,332)	    3,806</p>
<p>    Proposed dividend		     --		  157</p>
<p>(Loss)/ earnings per share before</p>
<p>    extraordinary item and tax (cents) (10.49)	 10.07</p>
<p>(Loss)/earnings per share after</p>
<p>    extraordinary item and tax (cents)  (4.66)	  7.61</p>
<p>NOTES: Cyprus Airways Limited is a government controlled company with 20 percent of its shares floated on the Cyprus Stock Exchange. The group is comprised of the following companies:</p>
<p>Cyprus Airways Limited</p>
<p>Eurocypria Airlines Limited</p>
<p>Cyprair Tours Limited</p>
<p>Cyprus Airways (Duty Free) Limited</p>
<p>* The extraordinary item represents the return of fees paid by Cyprus Airways to Eurocontrol, the air traffic control association of Europe, between 1991 and 1995. The Cypriot government, which receives a portion of Eurocontrol's proceeds, returned the money to the airline in the first half of 1996 on a one-off basis.</p>
<p>* Cyprus Airways took over the operation of duty free shops at the island's airports in May 1996. Turnover of the shops, put at 13.3 million pounds, is not included in the turnover figures of the group.</p>
<p>--- Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
</text>
